// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`lares nexus — every verb reaches its door > the three usage surfaces read byte-for-byte as they stand > kahuli usage 1`] = `
"lares nexus kahuli: unknown tier "not-a-tier"
usage: lares nexus kahuli <engine | grammar>

  the OVERTURN — advance one ratchet tier of this Nexus's genesis composition:
    engine   the SLOW ratchet: the hearth true-name (engineCid), signed into every device
             delegation edge — it binds MEMBERSHIP. HELD: advancing re-binds the fleet mesh-wide;
             the graceful forward-rebind span (predecessor + both-epoch reads) awaits its rulings.
    grammar  the FAST ratchet: the REQUIRED memetic-wikitext grammar alone (grammarCid) —
             never the true-name. Reads the current epoch; --apply re-derives the island (the bake).

  a read NEVER builds — the deliberate build+push lives behind --apply and in \`nexus rite kahuli\`."
`;

exports[`lares nexus — every verb reaches its door > the three usage surfaces read byte-for-byte as they stand > nexus usage 1`] = `
"lares nexus: unknown verb "definitely-not-a-verb"
usage: lares nexus <seal | rite | kapae | un_kapae | contract | revoke | carry | uncarry | members | accept-carriage | admit-take | carry-for | posture | kahuli | publish | realm-bag | realm-bags | offering>

lares nexus — the Nexus relation doors: charter ceremony, admission, carriage, posture, realm bags, and exact local offering inspection.

  seal <seat | rotate | show | export | import | grow | cold>  the kahu quorum's seats + pre-rotated epoch chain; grow = the crossing record ceremony; cold rehearse = read a card back
  kapae <nym> [--reason <text>]             raise a quorum-signed ban on a presenter nym
  kapae --list                              read the currently-Kapae'd set (the fold)
  un_kapae <nym>                            mint a quorum-signed causal lift
  contract <operator-pubkey> [--sig <hex>]  seat a vessel at the CONTRACT cap-tier (quorum + contract-in);
                                            --json emits the admit BUNDLE the joinee takes by hand
  revoke <operator-pubkey>                  revoke a member (quorum-only)
  carry <place-vessel-key> --carrier <hex>  contract a faceless PLACE (a Herm) as a CARRIER — quorum + its own
                                            VESSEL-key seal. It NEVER enters the member set; its whole grant is
                                            the realm's PUBLIC-declared books, by hash (heraldry#/the-herm-card)
  uncarry <place-vessel-key>                end a carrier contract (quorum-only)
  members --list [--nexus <aid>]            read a Nexus's members board — a public RECORD of admits, never
                                            authority (default: the primary charter's Nexus)
  accept-carriage [--index N] [--nexus <aid>]  (joining operator) mint + keep the 'accepts carriage' contract-in
                                            for one Nexus (default: the primary charter's)
  admit-take <bundle-file>                  (joining operator) verify the admit bundle a founding kahu handed over
                                            against the charter held for its Nexus, keep it, and re-present a
                                            running vessel's dial to the hearth that wrote it
  carry-for                                 (joining PLACE, on itself) mint the carrier seal with its OWN vessel
                                            key — reads no persona, because a crossroads holds none
  posture [private | open]                  read / flip the cross-Nexus federation posture
  rite <petname>                            the pet-named procedures — \`cabal\` seats the founding quorum, \`kahuli\` overturns a ratchet tier
  kahuli <engine | grammar>                 the OVERTURN — advance one ratchet tier of this Nexus's genesis composition
  realm-bag <bag-uri>                       register a bag this steward keeps on the realm's shared CRDT (read at CONTRACT);
                                            the WORN face's key for this Nexus seals it (\`lares persona wear N\` first)
            [--realm <id>]                  the realm the act lands in: a cabal realm (64 hex) or the charter-derived realm (the default)
            [--join]                        ASK to keep a bag another hand keeps — the record waits on each standing steward
            [--cosign [--with <key>]]       consent as a named steward to a record that waits on this hand;
                                            \`--with\` names the asker where several records wait
            [--steward <key>[,<key>]]       also NAME those stewards, each a key that already sealed a record of this realm
            [--tier contract|public]        the DECLARED read — public names a book the Herm carries by hash
            [--expiry <rolls>]              lease the registration against the realm's own pace
            [--charter <nym>=<realm-id>]    the charter a named hand holds (a book spanning two charters)
  publish <plugins>                         THE OFFERING DOOR — what THIS operator publishes for others to take;
                                            held apart from \`kahuli\`, which overturns what the MESH shares
  offering inspect <offering-cid>           inspect one exact local gift; read-only, no fetch or install
  realm-bags [--realm <id>]                 the bags a realm carries, and who keeps each; a listing never enters a realm

Examples:
  lares nexus rite quorum
  lares nexus contract <operator-pubkey> --json
  lares nexus admit-take ./admit-bundle.json
  lares nexus offering inspect sha256:<offering-cid>"
`;

exports[`lares nexus — every verb reaches its door > the three usage surfaces read byte-for-byte as they stand > seal usage 1`] = `
"lares nexus seal: unknown sub-verb "not-a-subverb"
usage: lares nexus seal <seat | rotate | show | export | import | grow | cold rehearse>

  seat    form the roster from the personas that STOOD for a chair, give each chair a seat key
          of its own, and establish the GENESIS epoch over those keys. Each chair's NEXT key mints
          as a cold key on a card: the card prints once, you type it back, and the genesis commits
          one digest per chair. No next key rests on this machine.
          [--threshold <k>]            the quorum rule (default: majority of those that stood)
  rotate  type back each chair's card: each revealed key becomes its chair's seat key, and the
          chain advances. The roster becomes exactly what STANDS — the succession door: a kahu
          steps down by no longer standing, a new one takes a chair by standing and signs with a
          fresh key. Fresh cards print for the rolled head, and you type them back.
          [--threshold <k>]  the quorum rule for the new roster (default: majority)
  show    read the kahu quorum's seats + chain head + quorum verdict + the carried set
  cold rehearse  type back one or more chairs' cards: each reads against the digests the head
          committed and names the chair it would roll. Nothing moves: no key, row or charter.
  import <file>          land a charter at the primary path — only where none stands, or the same one
  import --carry <file>  land a PARTNER's charter beside yours, under its Nexus AID; a re-import for
                         that AID lands only when its seal lineage extends the held head"
`;
